NavReceiverOnReportTest
├── when the caller is not the forwarder
│   └── it should revert
├── when the metadata is shorter than the workflow header
│   └── it should revert
├── when the workflow id does not match
│   └── it should revert
├── when the workflow owner does not match
│   └── it should revert
├── when the workflow name does not match
│   └── it should revert
├── given the owner disabled the identity checks
│   └── it should accept any workflow
├── when the report kind is unknown
│   └── it should revert
├── given a nav report
│   ├── when the version is unsupported
│   │   └── it should revert
│   ├── when the vault rejects the settlement
│   │   └── it should bubble the vault error up
│   └── when the vault accepts the settlement
│       └── it should settle the epoch and emit the report event
└── given a top up intent
    ├── when the version is unsupported
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when the route, the reason or the amount is invalid
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when the intent id was already recorded
    │   └── it should revert
    └── when the intent is new and valid
        └── it should record it and emit the event
